# Testing

Tests verify **real behavior**. Runner is `bun:test` (`bun test`). Do not add Jest or Vitest.

## Mock only at system boundaries

Do not mock internal modules, Zod schemas, Hono routes, or the MongoDB driver.

| Boundary | What to stub |
|----------|----------------|
| External HTTP | LLM / tax-engine / third-party APIs |
| Time | Clock injection when the assertion depends on it |
| Filesystem | Specific file reads, not the whole module |

Persistence tests use the real driver via `connectDb()` (in-memory Mongo when `MONGODB_URI` is unset). Clean up documents you insert. Do not `vi.fn()` — if you must stub a seam, use `mock` from `bun:test`.

## What to test

Always: Zod valid/invalid/edges, route status + JSON shape, Mongo round-trip through the schema, review accept/reject/edit, empty/loading/error UI, client-scoped reads, honest-failure envelopes.

Skip: trivial getters, generated code, thin third-party wrappers.

## Assertions

Assert on status, bodies, persisted docs, rendered UI. Never "mock was called" as the only assertion. Do not pin exact LLM prose — pin structure (status, fields, citations, confidence, incomplete envelope).

## TDD

Red (right reason) → green (minimum) → refactor. See `.cursor/skills/red-green-tdd/SKILL.md`. Gate: `bun run typecheck && bun test && bun run build`.

## Anti-patterns

Mocking `MongoClient` or `recordsCollection`. Tests that pass if errors are swallowed. Fixtures that skip `schema.parse`. Claiming done without exercising the review flow the user sees.
